node.doctext:
Dear monkers, I need a permanent prompt to listen for user commands. The code I'm currently using is the following:<br />

<code>sub promptUser {
   local($promptString,$defaultValue) = @_;
   print $promptString;
   $| = 1;          
   $_ = <STDIN>;      
   chomp;
   return $_;
}
while (1) {
$command = &promptUser("ABC> ");
}</code>
<br />
The above code works perfect, and store what user write into $command variable. The problem is that in this prompt, Backspace and arrows doesn't work. I got something like: <b>^H^[[A^[[B</b> . So for delete chars I have to use canc, but I cannot use arrows to move into what I wrote or UP and DOWN to surf into history like bash already do.
Is there a way to use backspace and/or arrows without external module? (I'm in a server offline)<br />
Thank you Lucas
